sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If a rational area is applied to a rational straight line, then it produces as breadth a straight line rational and commensurable in length with the straight line to which it is applied.
----
proof:

Let the rational area {AC|ACh} be applied to {AB}, a straight line once more rational in any of the aforesaid ways, producing {BC} as breadth.

